---
// One patient's record, in the workspace (the Patients tab lit), as a digital copy of a Philippine clinic's paper
// patient record (the owner, 3 Oct 2026: "make the patient records as simple as this, better a digital copy of the
// real form", then "make it a better but still simple like that"). The paper's layout, labels and order, kept as
// plain; better only where a screen is plainly better: a box you tap to change it, the age worked out from the birth
// date, allergies in red, the balance computed, the letterhead filled in.
//
//   The head (above the paper): ‹ Patients, the actions (New booking, the one teal button; Edit details; Print the
//   record; More), the safety chips, the note for the dentist, what a post did, and the contents (./_record/RecordNav).
//   Page 1 of 3: today's visit as a note clipped to the front (./_record/VisitStrip), the letterhead (THIS clinic's
//   own name, address, phone and email; Chart # and Date: ./_record/Letterhead), the Patient's chart (the
//   odontogram with the paper's codes and legend), the Patient information record: Basic information in the paper's
//   order and words, HMO, emergency contact and the desk note under it, the Dental history, the Medical history
//   (./_record/PaperHistory) and blood pressure.
//   Page 2 of 3: Informed consent: the privacy notice (DeskConsent, one ruled line once it is on record), then the
//   paper's ten paragraphs with our forms for each, the general consent with the paper's foot, and the history under it
//   (./_record/ConsentForms). Page 3 of 3: the Treatment record (the paper's ledger, ./_record/TreatmentRecord).
//   Attached to this record (./_record/Attached): Treatment, Clinical notes, Prescriptions and letters, X-rays and
//   files, Appointments (with the next check-up), Account (finance.bill only), Texts, each folded to one line until
//   it is opened, gone to by its address or contents link, or a post lands in it (the server draws it open).
// Every part keeps its region and ids (#rec-<id>, #overview, #health, #chart, #notes, #money …), so every address,
// post landing and side panel of before still lands. A post comes back to its part (data-rec-start). Money is shown
// only to people who may bill here (can(clinic, 'finance.bill')), like the Finances tab. "Print the record" prints the
// three pages as the paper is (record.css, "Printed"): black on white, each page on its own sheet, nothing else.
//
// Every query runs inside withClinic(), so row-level security decides whether
// this patient exists here; a patient of another clinic (or a made-up id) is
// a 404 on reading and on every post. Opening the record writes
// patient.view to the audit log.
//
// The odontogram is src/components/Odontogram.astro. It gains the palette's
// record actions, the plan/done marks, the paper's codes and legend and the
// baby teeth A–T (props `actions`, `work`, `codes`, `primary`); its
// offline logic (the kept copy of this page, changes waiting on the device)
// is untouched. A copy served offline opens on the Chart, and a notice the
// chart raises (a colleague's newer finding, changes waiting) brings the
// Chart forward. The palette's Add to plan, Treatment done and Clinical note
// open Add to plan, Record a treatment and the note (_record/TreatmentPanels,
// _record/NotePanel, outside the sections) over the Chart on that tooth; they
// post back=chart, and the save lands on the chart with its line (?back=chart).
//
// Four forms post back to this page, each with the CSRF token, checked before
// anything else (a miss comes back with ?stale=1):
//   intent=health   birth date, the paper's dental and medical history
//                   (answers.paper, src/lib/paper-history.ts), allergies,
//                   conditions, medicines, a note.
//                   saveHealth() in src/lib/health.ts: a new medical_history
//                   version under the person who saved it (a birth date
//                   change is kept in it, from and to), audit health.update /
//                   patient.birth_date. A save that started from an older
//                   version than the newest, or that changes a birth date
//                   someone else changed since, writes nothing and shows what
//                   the other person saved.
//   intent=consent  the privacy notice agreed at the desk (DeskConsent.astro),
//                   recordDeskConsent(): channel 'desk', who agreed (the
//                   patient, or a parent or guardian, named), audit
//                   consent.desk. Under 18 by the birth date on file, only a
//                   parent or guardian; with none on file, the desk says which.
//   intent=paper    a consent signed on paper (recordPaperConsent): a printed
//                   copy of the notice in force, dated on a day it was in
//                   force, or the clinic's own form (026). Audit consent.paper
//                   / consent.paper_form.
//   intent=details  Edit details (a side panel): name, chart no., sex, occupation,
//                   mobile, email, address, the parent or guardian, HMO,
//                   emergency contact, notes — updateDetails() in src/lib/import.ts,
//                   audit patient.update. Occupation and the guardian are read
//                   only from a form that drew them (has_paper_fields).
//                   The birth date stays with the health form, which keeps its
//                   history. Opened from the Dashboard's desk note
//                   (?open=details&dash=<visit>), the form carries the visit in
//                   a hidden dash, and a save goes back to the Dashboard with that
//                   visit open (only a visit of this patient's).
//   intent=printed  sent by the page as it prints (Print the record, or the
//                   browser's own Print): audit record.print, nothing else.
// All but the last need staff_access.can_edit_records for this branch (every role has it
// today; see canEditRecords()). On success the page redirects to itself
// (?saved=…) so a reload does not post again; on a problem it renders again
// with what was typed.
//
// Patient forms (the QR code on the desk, src/lib/patient-forms.ts): a form
// added to this record comes here with ?saved=form&form=<id>, and the page
// says what it wrote (the consents as the record now has them: from the form,
// already on file, or none because the record makes the patient a minor who
// signed for themself; the allergies, conditions and medicines kept from the
// record), and lists each detail the form says differently, or a mobile or
// email the desk did not tick, with "Use <it>" (a fifth post, intent
// form-use: useFormDetail writes that one detail and comes back with
// &used=<field>). Names and the birth date are never offered. The page
// says what went on the record and, for a patient already on file, what the
// form says differently (kept as on file; Edit details changes it). The
// Dental history shows what the patient's own forms say where the desk has no
// answer (the reason for the visit, what is bothering them); Consent lists every form added here — when it was sent,
// who signed, the consents it wrote — with its answers and a printout
// (../forms/<id>/). A health version from a form reads "from the patient
// forms (QR-7K2F)".
export const prerender = false;

import ClinicLayout from '../../../../layouts/Clinic.astro';
import Csrf from '../../../../components/Csrf.astro';
import DeskConsent from '../../../../components/DeskConsent.astro';
import ConsentForms from './_record/ConsentForms.astro';
import Odontogram from '../../../../components/Odontogram.astro';
import Pane from '../../../../components/ws/Pane.astro';
import Chip from '../../../../components/ws/Chip.astro';
import Empty from '../../../../components/ws/Empty.astro';
import SidePanel from '../../../../components/ws/SidePanel.astro';
import Icon from '../../../../components/ws/Icon.astro';
import Menu from '../../../../components/ws/Menu.astro';
import Head from './_ui/Head.astro';
import Callout from './_ui/Callout.astro';
import Glyph from './_ui/Glyph.astro';
import './_ui/patients.css';
import './_forms/forms.css';
import './_record/record.css';
import TreatmentRecord from './_record/TreatmentRecord.astro';
import VisitPanels from './_record/VisitPanels.astro';
import TreatmentPanels from './_record/TreatmentPanels.astro';
import ChartOffer from './_record/ChartOffer.astro';
import NotePanel from './_record/NotePanel.astro';
import Treatment from './_record/Treatment.astro';
import Notes from './_record/Notes.astro';
import Prescriptions from './_record/Prescriptions.astro';
import Files from './_record/Files.astro';
import RecallCard from './_record/RecallCard.astro';
import Vitals from './_record/Vitals.astro';
import Letters from './_record/Letters.astro';
import Loas from './_record/Loas.astro';
import PayPlans from './_record/PayPlans.astro';
import RecordNav from './_record/RecordNav.astro';
import Banner from './_record/Banner.astro';
import Plus from './_record/Plus.astro';
import FormCell from './_record/FormCell.astro';
import Who from './_record/Who.astro';
import VisitStrip from './_record/VisitStrip.astro';
import Letterhead from './_record/Letterhead.astro';
import Attached from './_record/Attached.astro';
import PaperHistory from './_record/PaperHistory.astro';
import PaperHistoryFields from './_record/PaperHistoryFields.astro';
import { shellLinks } from '../../../../components/ws/routes';
import { requireWorkspace } from '../../../../lib/workspace';
import { withClinic } from '../../../../lib/db';
import { csrfOk, csrfToken, CSRF_MESSAGE } from '../../../../lib/csrf';
import { hit, waitText, LIMITS } from '../../../../lib/throttle';
import {
  LISTS, NOTE_MAX, NAME_MAX, manilaToday, ageOn, ageText, when, day, oneLine, readHealthForm, saveHealth, readHealth,
  canEditRecords, readConsents, noticeInForce, recordDeskConsent, versionChanges, listText, answered, dateText, capitalise,
  consentInForce, readPaperForms, readPaperForm, recordPaperConsent, PAPER_WORDS, recheckHealth,
  type HealthAnswers, type HealthVersion, type AgreedAs, type PaperIn,
} from '../../../../lib/health';
import { readPersonForm, updateDetails, hmoSuggestions, SEXES, NOTES_MAX, OCCUPATION_MAX, GUARDIAN_NAME_MAX, RELATION_MAX, type PersonIn } from '../../../../lib/import';
import { asksPregnancy, showsPregnancy, rebasePaper, FIELD, paperValueText, type PaperTyped } from '../../../../lib/paper-history';
import { pesos, statementNo, STATUS as BILL_STATUS, fromDb } from '../../../../lib/invoices';
import { prettyPhone } from '../../../../lib/messages';
import { hmos } from '../../../../data/directory';
import { type ToothCondition, type ToothMark, type Surface, type Notation } from '../../../../data/demo';
import { patientForms, getForm, compareWithRecord, useFormDetail, healthLists, TAKEABLE, type FormConsentState } from '../../../../lib/patient-forms';
import { can } from '../../../../lib/can';
import { mayManage } from '../../../../lib/roles';
import type { PtrFix } from '../../../../lib/ptr';
import { loadClinical, loadChartChanges, recordAction, RECORD_INTENTS, RX_ROWS, type Outcome, type RecordProblem, type RxItem } from '../../../../lib/record';
import { loadExtra, extraAction, bpWords, EXTRA_INTENTS, EXTRA_ANCHOR } from '../../../../lib/record-extra';
import { loadVisitConsents, treatmentInForce } from '../../../../lib/visit-consent';
import { Refused } from '../../../../lib/refused';
import { loadConsentDocuments, mayAttest, capacityNote, consentGapsFor, overrideConsent } from '../../../../lib/consent-docs';
import { intakeGates, intakeAnswers, useIntakeDetail } from '../../../../lib/intake';
import { loadVisits, type StripVisit } from '../../../../lib/visit-record';
import { buildLedger, loadLedgerMoney, loadRecallsSet } from '../../../../lib/treatment-record';
import { offerFor } from '../../../../lib/chart-write';
import { calloutWorthy, isOnChart } from '../../../../lib/chart-offer';
import { chartSession } from '../../../api/chart';
import { PLACE, settingsAt } from '../../../../lib/places';

const ws = await requireWorkspace(Astro);
if (ws instanceof Response) return ws;
const { clinic, session, branches } = ws;
const money = can(clinic, 'finance.bill');
const links = shellLinks(clinic.slug);

const UUID = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;
const patientId = Astro.params.patient ?? '';
const notFound = () => new Response('No such patient', { status: 404 });
if (!UUID.test(patientId)) return notFound();
const here = `/c/${clinic.slug}/patients/${patientId}/`;
const HMO_NAMES = new Map(hmos.map((h) => [h.id, h.name]));
const q = Astro.url.searchParams;
// The tag of this sign-in (the chart's own): a chart write from the record is made only from a page drawn under it (p01 step 2).
const chartSid = chartSession(session);

// What a post left behind for the page to show.
let healthProblems: string[] = [];
let posted: { answers: HealthAnswers; birth: string; birthWas: string; base: string; paperTyped: PaperTyped } | null = null;
let conflict: { latest: HealthVersion | null; birth: string | null; versionMoved: boolean; birthMoved: boolean; paperClash: string[] } | null = null;
let consentProblem: string | null = null;
let givenBy = '';
let agreedAs: AgreedAs | null = null;
let paperState: { open: boolean; problem: string | null; values: Partial<PaperIn> } = { open: false, problem: null, values: {} };
let detailsProblems: string[] = [];
let detailsPosted: PersonIn | null = null;
// Edit details opened from the Dashboard (?open=details&dash=<visit>): the visit to go back to once it is saved.
let detailsDash: string | null = null;
let formUseProblem: string | null = null;
// A Go ahead anyway from the This visit strip (intent consent-override) that was refused: which form, so its panel opens again.
let aheadDoc: string | null = null;
// A clinical-record post (Treatment, Notes, Prescriptions, Files, the next check-up) that was refused.
let recordProblem: RecordProblem | null = null;
let rxTyped: RxItem[] = [];
// "No change" on the This visit strip (intent health-checked) that was refused: its sentence, on the strip.
let stripProblem: string | null = null;
// The section a post came back to.
let backTo: string | null = null;
// Where on the page a clinical-record post lands again.
const ANCHOR: Record<string, string> = { 'done-add': 'treatment-done', 'lab-add': 'treatment-lab', 'lab-next': 'treatment-lab', 'recall-set': 'recall', 'recall-done': 'recall', 'recall-clear': 'recall' };
/** The part of the record a clinical-record intent or saved word belongs to, by its first word (plan-done, rx:<id>, files:3,
 *  recall-cleared …): where a post lands, and the attached sheet the server draws open for it (a refused post's panel is in
 *  it, and a dialog in a closed sheet is not drawn). The next check-up is on Appointments. */
const PART_OF: Record<string, string> = {
  plan: 'treatment', done: 'treatment', lab: 'treatment', loa: 'treatment', payplan: 'treatment', adjust: 'treatment', adjusted: 'treatment', charted: 'treatment',
  note: 'notes', addendum: 'notes', rx: 'rx', letter: 'rx', answered: 'rx', file: 'files', files: 'files', recall: 'visits', vitals: 'health', chart: 'chart',
};
const partOf = (s: string | null | undefined) => PART_OF[(s ?? '').split(/[-:]/)[0]] ?? null;
/** A refused clinical-record post (src/lib/refused.ts): thrown out of the transaction so nothing half-done is kept, its outcome as the detail. */
type RecordRefusal = Extract<Outcome, { ok: false }>;

if (Astro.request.method === 'POST') {
  const form = await Astro.request.formData();
  if (!csrfOk(Astro.cookies, form)) return Astro.redirect(here + '?stale=1', 303);
  const intent = String(form.get('intent') ?? '');
  // Same allowance as the chart: a person saving never meets it; a script does.
  const rate = await hit('record:s:' + session.staffId, ...LIMITS.chart.staff);
  const slow = rate.allowed ? null : 'Too many saves at once. ' + waitText(rate.retryAfter);
  // The visit a chairside post was for (036): the This visit strip's forms and the panels it opens carry it,
  // and the page comes back with ?visit=<id> kept, so the strip is still there after the save.
  const postedVisit = UUID.test(String(form.get('visit') ?? '')) ? String(form.get('visit')) : null;
  const to = (qs: string, hash: string) => `${here}?${[postedVisit ? `visit=${postedVisit}` : '', qs].filter(Boolean).join('&')}${hash ? `#${hash}` : ''}`;

  if (intent === 'printed') {
    // The page as it prints (Print the record, or the browser's own Print): who printed this record, and when. Sent by
    // the page's script with navigator.sendBeacon, which reads no answer.
    if (rate.allowed) await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => {
      if ((await tx.query('select 1 from patient where id = $1', [patientId])).rowCount)
        await tx.query(`insert into audit_log (clinic_id, staff_id, action, entity, entity_id) values ($1, $2, 'record.print', 'patient', $3)`, [clinic.id, session.staffId, patientId]);
    });
    return new Response(null, { status: 204 });
  } else if (intent === 'health') {
    backTo = 'health';
    const { answers, birth, paper, paperTyped, problems } = readHealthForm(form);
    let paperShown = paperTyped;
    let base = String(form.get('base') ?? '');
    // The birth date this page opened with: a save changes the birth date only when this person changed it.
    let birthWas = oneLine(form.get('birth_was'));
    let birthShown = oneLine(form.get('birth_date'));
    if (slow) problems.unshift(slow);
    if (problems.length === 0) {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? saveHealth(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, base, answers, birth, birthWas: birthWas || null, paper })
          : ({ kind: 'denied' } as const));
      if (r.kind === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r.kind === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(to(`saved=${r.answers ? 'health' : 'birth'}`, 'health'), 303);
      if (r.kind === 'unchanged') return Astro.redirect(to('saved=nothing', 'health'), 303);
      if (r.kind === 'denied') problems.push('Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.');
      if (r.kind === 'conflict') {
        // The paper's answers come back as they are on file now, with only this person's own changes kept, so the next
        // Save does not put an old answer back over a colleague's (paper-history.ts rebasePaper); where both changed the
        // same question, the callout names what is on file.
        const re = rebasePaper(paperTyped, paper, r.basePaper, r.latest?.paper ?? null);
        paperShown = re.typed;
        const paperClash = re.clash.map((k) => `${FIELD[k].long} ${paperValueText(FIELD[k], r.latest?.paper?.[k] ?? null) ?? 'not asked'}`);
        conflict = { latest: r.latest, birth: r.birth, versionMoved: (r.latest?.id ?? 'none') !== base, birthMoved: (r.birth ?? '') !== birthWas, paperClash };
        // The next Save starts from what is on file now. A birth date this person
        // did not change shows the one on file; one they changed stays as typed.
        if (birthShown === birthWas) birthShown = r.birth ?? '';
        base = r.latest?.id ?? 'none';
        birthWas = r.birth ?? '';
      }
    }
    healthProblems = problems;
    posted = { answers, birth: birthShown, birthWas, base, paperTyped: paperShown };
  } else if (intent === 'consent') {
    backTo = 'consent';
    givenBy = oneLine(form.get('given_by_name'));
    const who = String(form.get('agreed_as') ?? '');
    agreedAs = who === 'patient' || who === 'guardian' ? who : null;
    if (slow) consentProblem = slow;
    else if (form.get('agreed') !== '1') consentProblem = 'Tick the box that says they agreed, once they have. Nothing was recorded.';
    else if (givenBy.length > NAME_MAX) consentProblem = `Keep the name under ${NAME_MAX} characters.`;
    else {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? recordDeskConsent(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, version: String(form.get('version') ?? ''), givenBy: givenBy || null, agreedAs })
          : ('denied' as const));
      if (r === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=consent#consent`, 303);
      if (r === 'already') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=consent-already#consent`, 303);
      consentProblem = {
        denied: 'Your account cannot record consent at this branch. Ask the owner.',
        who: 'Choose who is agreeing: the patient, 18 or over, or a parent or guardian. Nothing was recorded.',
        minor: 'The birth date on file makes the patient under 18, so a parent or guardian agrees for them. Ask them to type their name. Nothing was recorded.',
        'guardian-name': 'A parent or guardian is agreeing, so they type their name. Nothing was recorded.',
        'no-notice': 'No privacy notice is in force, so there is nothing to record.',
        changed: 'The privacy notice changed while this page was open. Show the patient the new one below.',
      }[r];
      if (r === 'minor') agreedAs = 'guardian';
    }
  } else if (intent === 'paper') {
    backTo = 'consent';
    const { paper, problems } = readPaperForm(form);
    paperState = { open: true, problem: slow ?? (problems.length ? problems.join(' ') : null), values: paper };
    if (!paperState.problem) {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? recordPaperConsent(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, ...paper })
          : ('denied' as const));
      if (r === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=paper#consent-paper`, 303);
      paperState.problem = r === 'denied' ? 'Your account cannot record consent at this branch. Ask the owner.' : `${PAPER_WORDS[r]} Nothing was recorded.`;
    }
  } else if (intent === 'details') {
    backTo = 'overview';
    const { person, problems } = readPersonForm(form);
    detailsPosted = person;
    const dashIn = String(form.get('dash') ?? '');
    detailsDash = UUID.test(dashIn) ? dashIn.toLowerCase() : null;
    if (slow) problems.unshift(slow);
    if (!problems.length) {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id))
          ? updateDetails(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, p: person })
          : ('denied' as const));
      if (r === 'none') return notFound();
      if (r === 'saved' && detailsDash) {
        // Back to the Dashboard with that visit's panel open, showing the new note: only a visit of this patient's.
        const v = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => (await tx.query(
          `select to_char(starts_at at time zone 'Asia/Manila', 'YYYY-MM-DD') as ymd from appointment where id = $1 and patient_id = $2`, [detailsDash, patientId])).rows[0]);
        if (v) return Astro.redirect(`/c/${clinic.slug}/?${v.ymd === manilaToday() ? '' : `date=${v.ymd}&`}booking=${detailsDash}`, 303);
      }
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=details#overview`, 303);
      problems.push(r === 'denied' ? 'Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.' : r.taken);
    }
    detailsProblems = problems;
  } else if (RECORD_INTENTS.has(intent) || EXTRA_INTENTS.has(intent)) {
    // The clinical record (src/lib/record.ts): every intent checks canEditRecords in its own transaction.
    // A panel opened from the chart's palette posts back=chart: saved or refused, it comes back to the Chart.
    const postedBack = form.get('back') === 'chart' ? 'chart' : form.get('back') === 'treatment' ? 'treatment' : null;
    const outcome = slow
      ? ({ ok: false, section: 'overview', problem: slow, values: {} } as Extract<Outcome, { ok: false }>)
      : await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => {
          const o = EXTRA_INTENTS.has(intent)
            ? await extraAction(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, canBill: money, hmoNames: HMO_NAMES }, intent, form)
            : await recordAction(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, sid: chartSid }, intent, form);
          if (o !== 'none' && !o.ok) throw new Refused<RecordRefusal>(o.problem, o);
          return o;
        }).catch((e) => { if (e instanceof Refused) return (e as Refused<RecordRefusal>).detail; throw e; });
    if (outcome === 'none') return notFound();
    if (outcome.ok) {
      // A treatment the chart could show lands on its offer (treated=…, #chart-offer), in the section the post came from.
      const qs = [`saved=${encodeURIComponent(outcome.saved)}`, ...Object.entries(outcome.qs ?? {}).map(([k, v]) => `${k}=${encodeURIComponent(v)}`), postedBack === 'chart' ? 'back=chart' : ''].filter(Boolean).join('&');
      const hash = outcome.qs?.treated ? 'chart-offer' : postedBack === 'chart' ? 'chart' : ANCHOR[intent] ?? EXTRA_ANCHOR[intent] ?? outcome.section;
      return Astro.redirect(to(qs, hash), 303);
    }
    // Refused (the rate limit too): back to the part the form was posted from (partOf: the next check-up is on Appointments now).
    backTo = postedBack ?? (slow ? null : partOf(intent) ?? outcome.section);
    recordProblem = { intent, text: outcome.problem, values: outcome.values };
    if (intent === 'rx-add') {
      const col = (k: string) => form.getAll(k).map((x) => String(x));
      const [dr, st, qt, sg] = [col('drug'), col('strength'), col('qty'), col('sig')];
      rxTyped = Array.from({ length: RX_ROWS }, (_, i) => ({ drug: dr[i] ?? '', strength: st[i] ?? '', qty: qt[i] ?? '', sig: sg[i] ?? '' }));
    }
  } else if (intent === 'health-checked') {
    // "No change" on the This visit strip: the health history asked again today and still true (recheckHealth).
    if (slow) stripProblem = slow;
    else {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) =>
        (await canEditRecords(tx, session.staffId, clinic.id)) ? recheckHealth(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId }) : ('denied' as const));
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(to('saved=checked', ''), 303);
      if (r === 'today') return Astro.redirect(to('saved=checked-today', ''), 303);
      stripProblem = r === 'denied' ? 'Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.'
        : `There is no health history on file to check yet. Ask the patient and save the answers in ${PLACE.medicalHistory}.`;
    }
  } else if (intent === 'form-use') {
    // One detail from an added patient form onto the record ("Use 0917 555 0199").
    backTo = 'overview';
    const formId = String(form.get('form') ?? '');
    const field = String(form.get('field') ?? '');
    if (slow) formUseProblem = slow;
    else if (!UUID.test(formId) || !TAKEABLE.has(field)) formUseProblem = 'That detail cannot be taken from the form. Nothing was changed.';
    else {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, (tx) => useFormDetail(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, formId, field }));
      if (r === 'saved' || r === 'same') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?form=${formId}&used=${encodeURIComponent(field)}#overview`, 303);
      formUseProblem = r === 'not-allowed' ? 'Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.' : 'That form is not on this record any more. Nothing was changed.';
    }
  } else if (intent === 'intake-use') {
    // One detail from page 1 of an intake added to this record ("Use Teacher"), the QR forms' rule (phase 4.3).
    backTo = 'overview';
    const intakeId = String(form.get('intake') ?? '');
    const field = String(form.get('field') ?? '');
    if (slow) formUseProblem = slow;
    else if (!UUID.test(intakeId) || !TAKEABLE.has(field)) formUseProblem = 'That detail cannot be taken from the forms. Nothing was changed.';
    else {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, (tx) => useIntakeDetail(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, patientId, intakeId, field }));
      if (r === 'saved' || r === 'same') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?intake=${intakeId}&used=${encodeURIComponent(field)}#overview`, 303);
      formUseProblem = r === 'not-allowed' ? 'Your account cannot change records at this branch. Ask the owner.' : 'Those forms are not on this record any more. Nothing was changed.';
    }
  } else if (intent === 'consent-override') {
    // Go ahead anyway, from the This visit strip: the visit goes ahead without a consent form agreed, the reason kept with the
    // form (overrideConsent, context strip; phase 4.4). Comes back to the strip (?visit=).
    const docId = String(form.get('document') ?? '');
    const visitId = String(form.get('visit') ?? '');
    aheadDoc = UUID.test(docId) ? docId : null;
    if (slow) stripProblem = slow;
    else if (!aheadDoc || !UUID.test(visitId)) stripProblem = 'Choose the form. Nothing was recorded.';
    else {
      const r = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => {
        const own = (await tx.query('select 1 from consent_document where id = $1 and patient_id = $2 and appointment_id = $3 and cancelled_at is null', [docId, patientId, visitId])).rowCount;
        if (!own) throw new Refused('That form is not this visit’s any more. Nothing was recorded.');
        await overrideConsent(tx, { clinicId: clinic.id, staffId: session.staffId, docId, context: 'strip', reason: String(form.get('reason') ?? '') });
        return 'saved' as const;
      }).catch((e) => { if (e instanceof Refused) return e.reasons.join(' '); throw e; });
      if (r === 'saved') return Astro.redirect(`${here}?saved=consent-ahead&visit=${visitId}`, 303);
      stripProblem = r;
    }
  }
}

const data = await withClinic(clinic.id, async (tx) => {
